() Tj
T*
(  Mission Brief) Tj
T*
T*
(Welcome, Recruit. Before we dive into building agents, you need a firm grasp of the AI) Tj
T*
(concepts that power them. This mission will equip you with foundational knowledge of) Tj
T*
(conversational AI, large language models \(LLMs\), retrieval-augmented generation \(RAG\), and) Tj
T*
(the types of agents you can create in Copilot Studio.) Tj
T*
T*
(  Objectives) Tj
T*
T*
(In this mission, you ll learn:) Tj
T*
T*
(1. What conversational AI is and why it matters) Tj
T*
(1. How Large Language Models \(LLMs\) power chat experiences) Tj
T*
(1. What Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) brings to the table) Tj
T*
(1. The distinction between conversational agents and autonomous agents) Tj
T*
(1. How agents in Copilot Studio leverage these concepts) Tj
T*
T*
(Let s dive in!) Tj
T*
T*
(---) Tj
T*
T*
(What Is Conversational AI?) Tj
T*
T*
(Conversational AI refers to any system that can understand, process, and respond to human) Tj
T*
(language   whether text or speech   in a way that feels natural. Think chatbots in help) Tj
T*
(desks or virtual personal assistants in your favorite apps. Under the hood, most modern) Tj
T*
(conversational AIs rely on Large Language Models \(LLMs\), which we ll cover next.) Tj
T*
T*
(Why It Matters) Tj
T*
T*
(- User Experience: Conversational interfaces are often more intuitive than clicking) Tj
T*
(  through menus.) Tj
T*
(- Scalability: One agent can handle tens or hundreds of concurrent conversations.) Tj
T*
(- Efficiency: Instead of building custom rule-based scripts, LLM-powered agents adapt on) Tj
T*
(  the fly to user input.) Tj
T*
(- Extensibility: With the right design, agents can tap into knowledge bases, connect to) Tj
T*
(  APIs, or act as  digital coworkers  inside business workflows.) Tj
T*
T*
(---) Tj
T*
T*
(Large Language Models \(LLMs\) 101) Tj
T*
T*
(At the core of most conversational AI systems are Large Language Models   neural networks) Tj
T*
(trained on massive text corpora. They learn statistical patterns of language so they can) Tj
T*
(generate coherent sentences, answer questions, or even brainstorm ideas. Key points to) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
130 0 obj
<< /Length 2459 >>
stream
BT
/F1 12 Tf
14 TL
1 0 0 1 72 720 Tm
(understand:) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Training Data: LLMs ingest terabytes of text \(web pages, books, articles\). This  world) Tj
T*
(   knowledge  lets them respond on many topics.) Tj
T*
(1. Tokenization: Text is broken into smaller units called tokens \(words, subwords, or) Tj
T*
(   characters\). The model predicts one token at a time.) Tj
T*
(1. Context Window: Each LLM has a limit on how many tokens it can  see  at once. Beyond) Tj
T*
(   that limit, prior tokens get truncated.) Tj
T*
(1. Prompting: You interact with an LLM by sending it a prompt. The better your prompt, the) Tj
T*
(   more focused and relevant the response.) Tj
T*
(1. Zero-shot vs. Fine-tuning: Zero-shot means using an LLM as-is \(just raw weights\).) Tj
T*
(   Fine-tuning means adjusting the model on domain-specific data so it answers more) Tj
T*
(   accurately for your needs.) Tj
T*
(A common analogy is that an LLM is like a  super-smart autocomplete.  It doesn t truly) Tj
T*
(understand meaning like a human brain, but it s extremely good at predicting the next best) Tj
T*
(word \(or phrase\) in a sequence.) Tj
T*
T*
(---) Tj
T*
T*
(Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\)) Tj
T*
T*
(When LLMs rely solely on static training data, they might hallucinate or become outdated.) Tj
T*
(RAG addresses this by letting the model  look up  fresh information before composing an) Tj
T*
(answer. At a high level, RAG works like this:) Tj
T*
T*
(1. User Query: A user asks a question \(e.g.,  What s the latest on Contoso s quarterly) Tj
T*
(   earnings? \).) Tj
T*
(1. Retriever Step: The system queries a knowledge source \(documents, internal databases,) Tj
T*
(   SharePoint libraries, etc.\) to find relevant passages.) Tj
T*
(1. Augmentation: Retrieved passages get appended to or prepended before the LLM prompt.) Tj
T*
(1. Generation: The LLM ingests both the user s question and the retrieved context, then) Tj
T*
(   generates a response that s grounded in up-to-date data.) Tj
T*
T*
(With RAG, your agent can call internal company wikis, plugin APIs, or search an FAQ) Tj
T*
(knowledge base and return answers that aren t limited to statically published model) Tj
T*
(parameters.) Tj
T*
T*
(---) Tj
T*
T*
(Conversational vs. Autonomous Agents) Tj
T*
T*
(In the context of Copilot Studio, the term agent can refer to multiple flavors of AI) Tj
T*
(assistants. It s helpful to draw a line between:) Tj
T*
T*
(Conversational Agents:) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
131 0 obj
<< /Length 2657 >>
stream
BT
/F1 12 Tf
14 TL
1 0 0 1 72 720 Tm
(- Primarily focus on two-way dialogue.) Tj
T*
(- Persist context across multiple turns of a conversation.) Tj
T*
(- Usually orchestrated via predefined flows or triggers \(e.g.,  If user says X, respond) Tj
T*
(  with Y \).) Tj
T*
(- Ideal for customer support, FAQs, guided interactions, scheduling, or simple Q&A.) Tj
T*
(  - Examples:) Tj
T*
(- A Teams chatbot that answers HR policy questions.) Tj
T*
(- A Power Virtual Agents bot on a SharePoint page to guide users through a form.) Tj
T*
T*
(Autonomous Agents:) Tj
T*
T*
(- Go beyond back-and-forth chat; they can take actions on behalf of the user.) Tj
T*
(- Use LLM reasoning loops \(think  plan   act   observe   replan \) to complete tasks.) Tj
T*
(- Hook into external tools or APIs \(e.g., call a Power Automate flow, send calendar) Tj
T*
(  invites, manipulate data in Dataverse\).) Tj
T*
(- Operate without constant human prompts once triggered, they can handle multi-step) Tj
T*
(  processes autonomously.) Tj
T*
(  - Examples:) Tj
T*
(- An agent that generates a travel itinerary, books flights, and emails confirmations.) Tj
T*
(- A  Meeting Summarizer  agent that joins a Teams call, transcribes it in real time, and) Tj
T*
(  writes an executive summary to OneNote.) Tj
T*
(Conversational agents wait for user input and stick to dialogue. Autonomous agents) Tj
T*
(proactively plan and execute a sequence of steps using broader tool access.) Tj
T*
T*
(---) Tj
T*
T*
(Agents in Copilot Studio) Tj
T*
T*
(Copilot Studio unifies both conversational and autonomous scenarios under one framework.) Tj
T*
(Here s how Copilot Studio helps you build agents:) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Visual Agent Designer: A low-code canvas to define prompts, memory, and tools for both) Tj
T*
(   chat and action workflows.) Tj
T*
(1. LLM Configurations: Select from various OpenAI models or Microsoft s enterprise-grade) Tj
T*
(   GPT to match your performance and cost needs.) Tj
T*
(1. Retrieval Connectors: Prebuilt integrations for SharePoint, OneDrive, Azure Cognitive) Tj
T*
(   Search, and Dataverse, enabling RAG out of the box.) Tj
T*
(1. Custom Tools & Functions: Define custom HTTP actions or Power Automate flows that your) Tj
T*
(   agent can invoke autonomously.) Tj
T*
(1. Multi-Modal Support: Beyond text, Copilot Studio agents can ingest images, files, or) Tj
T*
(   structured data to enrich context.) Tj
T*
(1. Publishing & Distribution: Once your agent is ready, you can publish it to Microsoft) Tj
T*
(   365 Copilot \(so users invoke it in Teams, SharePoint, Outlook, etc.\) or embed it as a) Tj
T*
(   standalone chat widget on a webpage.) Tj
T*
T*
(---) Tj
ET
