(1. Leverages Knowledge Sources to ground its answers in your organization s data.) Tj
T*
(1. Calls Tools \(Actions\) as needed to perform tasks sending messages, updating records, or) Tj
T*
(   invoking APIs.) Tj
T*
T*
(Under the hood, the orchestrator uses a generative planning approach: it decides which) Tj
T*
(steps to take, in what order, to fulfill a user request. If an action fails \(for example,) Tj
T*
(an email can t be sent\), the agent follows your exception-handling guidelines \(ask a) Tj
T*
(clarifying question or report the error\). Because the LLM adapts to conversation context,) Tj
T*
(the agent can maintain memory over multiple turns and incorporate new information as the) Tj
T*
(conversation unfolds.) Tj
T*
T*
(Visual Flow Example:) Tj
T*
T*
