T*
(  Why Prompts matter) Tj
T*
T*
(- They guide the agent s behavior.) Tj
T*
(- They help the agent understand what kind of conversation to have.) Tj
T*
(- A good prompt makes the agent more helpful and accurate.) Tj
T*
T*
(  Tips for writing a good prompt) Tj
T*
T*
(- Be clear and specific - say exactly what you want the agent to do.) Tj
T*
(- Think like the user - what will the user say? What should the agent reply?) Tj
T*
(- Include examples - if possible, give a sample interaction.) Tj
T*
T*
(  Example) Tj
T*
T*
(Let's say the HR team needs an agent to help with vacation requests.) Tj
T*
T*
(The prompt could be,  I want to build an agent that helps users submit a vacation request.) Tj
T*
(When a user says they want to request time off, the agent should ask for their name, the) Tj
T*
(start date of their vacation, the end date of their vacation, and their manager s name.) Tj
T*
(Once the user provides this information, the agent should save it to a SharePoint list) Tj
T*
(called  Vacation Requests  and post a notification in a dedicated Microsoft Teams) Tj
T*
(channel. ) Tj
T*
T*
(Why this prompt works:) Tj
T*
T*
(- Clearly states the goal - submit a vacation request) Tj
T*
(- Describes the user interaction - what the user says and what the agent should ask) Tj
T*
(- Lists the required data - name, start date, end date, manager) Tj
T*
(- Mentions where the data goes - a SharePoint list called Vacation Requests) Tj
T*
T*
(  OK, I've created my agent... how do I next ground it with knowledge?) Tj
T*
T*
(In Copilot Studio, knowledge sources are places where your agent can find information to) Tj
T*
(give better answers. When you add these sources, your agent can pull in your enterprise) Tj
T*
(data from places like Power Platform, Dynamics 365, websites, and other systems or) Tj
T*
(services your company uses.) Tj
T*
T*
(These sources work together with AI to help your agent respond more accurately to user) Tj
T*
(questions, this is achieved through what is known as generative orchestration.) Tj
T*
T*
(  What is generative orchestration in the context of agents?) Tj
T*
T*
(Generative orchestration means the agent uses AI to dynamically decide how to answer a) Tj
T*
(question by combining its built-in language skills with information from your added) Tj
T*
(knowledge sources.) Tj
ET
endstream
