(1. Implementing best practices for designing responsive and user-friendly adaptive cards) Tj
T*
T*
(  What is an Adaptive Card?) Tj
T*
T*
(An Adaptive Card is way to create interactive, visually rich UI elements that can be) Tj
T*
(embedded in apps like Microsoft Teams, Microsoft Outlook or agents. It is a structured) Tj
T*
(JSON object that defines the layout and content of a card:) Tj
T*
T*
(- What elements appear on the card - text, images, buttons) Tj
T*
(- How those elements are arranged) Tj
T*
(- What actions users can take such as submitting a form or opening a link) Tj
T*
T*
(Why Adaptive Cards matter in Copilot Studio) Tj
T*
T*
(Imagine you're building an agent that asks users for their name, email, or feedback. If) Tj
T*
(you just use plain text, the conversation can feel boring or hard to follow. That s where) Tj
T*
(Adaptive Cards come in!) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Makes conversations interactive - instead of sending text as messages to the user, you) Tj
T*
(   can show buttons, forms, images and more.) Tj
T*
(- Example: a card can ask the user to fill in their name and email in a clean form.) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Look great everywhere - Adaptive Cards automatically match the style of the app they're) Tj
T*
(   in, such as Microsoft 365 Copilot chat or Microsoft Teams. You don't need to worry) Tj
T*
(   about dark mode, font, or layouts - it adapts.) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Easy to build with JSON - you define the card using JSON code \(think recipe for the) Tj
T*
(   UI\). Copilot Studio helps you preview your card before adding it to the topic.) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Collect and use data - you can use the card to ask questions, collect answers, and use) Tj
T*
(   that data in the conversation flow.) Tj
T*
(- Example: Ask for a user's phone number, then show a confirmation card with their phone) Tj
T*
(  number.) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Boost user experience - cards make your agent feel more interactive. It's a more clean,) Tj
T*
(   clickable, and user-friendly type of interface.) Tj
T*
T*
(  Is JSON a person?) Tj
T*
T*
(Pronounced as "Jason," it's not a person  ) Tj
T*
T*
(JSON, otherwise known as JavaScript Object Notation is a lightweight format used to) Tj
T*
(structure data. It's easy to read and write, and looks like a series of key-value pairs) Tj
T*
(inside curly braces {}.) Tj
T*
T*
(This is one of the options to use when adding an adaptive card to your topic.) Tj
ET
endstream
