(  Best practices) Tj
T*
T*
(Here are some best practices for creating Adaptive Cards for agents in Copilot Studio.) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Keep it simple and focused) Tj
T*
( - Design cards with a clear purpose, don t overload them with too many elements.) Tj
T*
(- Use concise text and intuitive layouts to guide users through the interaction.) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Be intentional with inputs) Tj
T*
( - Include only the necessary input elements such as text, date choices, to avoid) Tj
T*
(   overwhelming users.) Tj
T*
(- Use labels to make inputs easy to understand.) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Structure for readability) Tj
T*
( - Use TextBlocks for headings and instructions.) Tj
T*
(- Group related elements using Containers or ColumnSets to improve visual flow.) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Make Action elements clear) Tj
T*
( - Use Action.Submit and or Action.OpenUrl with clear button titles like "Submit Request") Tj
T*
(   or "View Details") Tj
T*
(- Avoid vague labels like "Click here") Tj
T*
T*
(1. Design for adaptability) Tj
T*
( - Assume the card may be viewed on different screen sizes.) Tj
T*
(- Avoid fixed widths and use flexible layouts like ColumnSets for responsiveness.) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Use dynamic content when possible) Tj
T*
( - Bind card elements to variables or outputs from nodes using Power Fx to personalize the) Tj
T*
(   user experience.) Tj
T*
(- For example, show the user's name or current status dynamically.) Tj
T*
T*
