<< /Length 2402 >>
stream
BT
/F1 12 Tf
14 TL
1 0 0 1 72 720 Tm
() Tj
T*
(  What is an Event Trigger?) Tj
T*
T*
(An Event Trigger is a mechanism that allows your agent to act autonomously in response to) Tj
T*
(external events, without requiring direct user input. Think of it as making your agent) Tj
T*
("watch" for specific events and automatically take action when those events occur.) Tj
T*
T*
(Unlike topic triggers, which require users to type something to activate a conversation,) Tj
T*
(event triggers activate based on things happening in your connected systems. E.g.:) Tj
T*
T*
(- When a new file is created in SharePoint or OneDrive for Business) Tj
T*
(- When a record is created in Dataverse) Tj
T*
(- When a task is completed in Planner) Tj
T*
(- When a new Microsoft Form response is submitted) Tj
T*
(- When a new Microsoft Teams message is added) Tj
T*
(- Based on a recurring schedule \(like daily reminders\)) Tj
T*
T*
(Why Event Triggers matter in autonomous agents) Tj
T*
T*
(Event triggers transform your agent from a reactive assistant into a proactive, autonomous) Tj
T*
(helper:) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Autonomous operation - your agent can work 24/7 without human intervention, responding) Tj
T*
(   to events as they happen.) Tj
T*
(- Example: Automatically welcome new team members when they're added to a team.) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Real-time responsiveness - instead of waiting for users to ask questions, your agent) Tj
T*
(   responds immediately to relevant events.) Tj
T*
(- Example: Alert the IT team when a SharePoint document is modified.) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Workflow automation - chain together multiple actions based on a single trigger event.) Tj
T*
(- Example: When a new support ticket is created, create a task, notify the manager, and) Tj
T*
(  update the tracking dashboard.) Tj
