stream
BT
/F1 12 Tf
14 TL
1 0 0 1 72 720 Tm
(autonomously to external events:) Tj
T*
T*
(The trigger workflow) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Event Detection - A specific event occurs in a connected system \(SharePoint, Teams,) Tj
T*
(   Outlook, etc.\)) Tj
T*
(1. Trigger Activation - The event trigger detects this event and sends a payload to your) Tj
T*
(   agent via a Power Automate Cloud Flow.) Tj
T*
(1. Agent Response - Your agent receives the payload and executes the instructions you've) Tj
T*
(   defined) Tj
T*
T*
(Event vs Topic triggers) Tj
T*
T*
(Understanding the difference between these two trigger types is crucial:) Tj
T*
T*
(| Event Triggers | Topic Triggers | |-------------------|-------------------| | Activated) Tj
T*
(by external system events | Activated by user input/phrases | | Enable autonomous agent) Tj
T*
(behavior | Enable conversational responses | | Use maker's authentication | Option for) Tj
T*
(user's authentication | | Run without user interaction | Require user to start) Tj
T*
(conversation | | Examples: File created, email received | Example: "What's the weather?" |) Tj
T*
T*
(  Understanding trigger payloads) Tj
T*
T*
(When an event occurs, the trigger sends a payload to your agent containing information) Tj
T*
(about the event and instructions on how to respond.) Tj
T*
T*
(Default vs custom payloads) Tj
T*
T*
(Every trigger type comes with a default payload structure, but you can customize it:) Tj
T*
T*
(Default payload - Uses the standard format like Use content from {Body}) Tj
T*
T*
(- Contains basic event information) Tj
T*
(- Uses generic processing instructions) Tj
T*
(- Good for simple scenarios) Tj
T*
T*
(Custom payload - Add specific instructions and data formatting) Tj
T*
T*
(- Include detailed directions for your agent) Tj
T*
(- Specify exactly what data to use and how) Tj
T*
(- Better for complex workflows) Tj
T*
T*
(Agent instructions vs custom payload instructions) Tj
T*
T*
(You have two places to guide your agent's behavior with event triggers:) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
