T*
T*
(  Lab 11: Publish your agent to Teams and Microsoft 365 Copilot) Tj
T*
T*
(  Use case) Tj
T*
T*
(Your Contoso IT Help Desk agent is now fully configured with powerful capabilities it can) Tj
T*
(access SharePoint knowledge sources, create support tickets, send proactive notifications,) Tj
T*
(and respond intelligently to user queries. However, all these features are currently only) Tj
T*
(available in the development environment where you built them.) Tj
T*
T*
(The Challenge: End users can't benefit from your agent's capabilities until it's properly) Tj
T*
(published and made accessible through the channels where they actually work.) Tj
T*
T*
(The Solution: Publishing your agent ensures that the latest version with all your recent) Tj
T*
(updates, new topics, enhanced knowledge sources, and configured flows is available to real) Tj
T*
(users. Without publishing, users would still interact with an older version of your agent) Tj
T*
(that might be missing critical functionality.) Tj
T*
T*
(Adding the Teams and Microsoft 365 Copilot channel is equally crucial because:) Tj
T*
T*
(- Teams Integration: Your organization's employees spend most of their day in Microsoft) Tj
T*
(  Teams for collaboration, meetings, and communication. By adding your agent to Teams,) Tj
T*
(  users can get IT support without leaving their primary work environment.) Tj
T*
T*
(- Microsoft 365 Copilot: Users can access your specialized IT help desk agent directly) Tj
T*
(  within their Microsoft 365 Copilot experience, making it seamlessly integrated into) Tj
ET
endstream
